mk-slackbuild.sh

mk-slackbuild.sh is a small helper script that generates a conservative
SlackBuild skeleton for Slackware and SlackBuilds.org.

It creates a standard directory layout containing:

  - PRGNAM.SlackBuild
  - PRGNAM.info
  - slack-desc
  - README

The generated SlackBuild follows traditional Slackware practices and
is intended to be edited by hand before use.


USAGE

  mk-slackbuild.sh <prgnam> [version]

If no version is provided, the placeholder value "UNKNOWN" is used.
This forces a manual review before building or submitting.


SCOPE

This script only generates a starting point.  It does not download
sources, resolve dependencies, or attempt to validate the build.

The slack-desc file is generated with placeholders and must be edited
manually.


INTENDED USE

This is a personal workflow tool for users already familiar with
SlackBuilds and shell scripting.  It is not part of SlackBuilds.org.

